## Available Skills & Triggers
When encountering specific engineering workflows, invoke the matching skill from `.agents/skills/`:
- `.agents/skills/orchestrator/`: Lead Project Orchestrator governing lifecycle gates G0-G6.
- `.agents/skills/project-discovery/`: Project initialization and environment inspection (`discovery`, `init`, Gate G0).
- `.agents/skills/requirements-analysis/`: Requirements specification and criteria formulation (`requirements`, Gate G1).
- `.agents/skills/existing-project-analysis/`: Brownfield codebase analysis and convention extraction.
- `.agents/skills/design-discovery/`: Design tokens, UI specifications, and accessibility (Gate G2).
- `.agents/skills/design-system-engineering/`: Design system tokens and component state auditing.
- `.agents/skills/architecture-and-contracts/`: System modeling, ADR drafting, interface contracts (Gate G3).
- `.agents/skills/phase-planning/`: Work breakdown structure, task scheduling, file ownership (WBS).
- `.agents/skills/controlled-implementation/`: Production code authoring within bounded file paths (Gate G4).
- `.agents/skills/testing-and-verification/`: Automated test execution, evidence capture, linter auditing.
- `.agents/skills/independent-review/`: Adversarial review of diffs, anti-slop verification (Gate G5).
- `.agents/skills/failure-recovery-and-improvement/`: Test failure diagnosis and regression fixing.
- `.agents/skills/cross-platform-adaptation/`: Platform compilation and instruction synchronization.
- `.agents/skills/documentation-and-handoff/`: 3-tier memory reconciliation, release notes, handoff (Gate G6).

---

## Subagent Delegation Protocol
When executing subagent workflows:
1. Maintain separate, isolated processes and context per subagent.
2. Assign disjoint, non-overlapping file ownership boundaries.
3. Subagents write execution results directly to contract JSON files and structured logs.
